# Any body part can attach radially (KSP-style): drag a Body tube from the Airframe bin over the booster's SIDE, away from an
# attach node, and it stands on the surface as a pod of the bin's symmetry count; over a node it stacks as before.
#   cargo run -q -p bowshock -- drive --example crates/bowshock/scripts/radial_tube.drive out/radial-tube
# The light theme: put `click "Prefs"`, `click "Light"`, `click "Done"` (Preferences > Appearance) after the viewport line.
viewport 1280x800
click (119, 705)
press "Body tube"
move (300, 560)
move (500, 400)
move (700, 300)
move (767, 276)
screenshot tube-ghost.png
release (767, 276)
screenshot tube-placed.png
click "2D"
screenshot tube-placed-2d.png
